Translated at the maintainer's direction (2026-09-28) into the kvim tab's
side-by-side editor + GitHub-flavoured Markdown preview. What was translated,
JavaScript/CSS -> Rust/egui, and where (each file carries its own provenance
header):

  - index.js `setOutput` (scroll the preview to the first changed element)
    and `update` (document title from the first h1)
      -> src/app/gfm_preview/model.rs `first_changed_block`, `document_title`
  - index.js `render_tasklist` (task items as disabled checkboxes)
      -> src/app/gfm_preview/view.rs `show_item`
  - index.css `#in`/`#out` (50/50 source|preview split) and index.js
    `toggleReadMode` (preview only)
      -> src/app/kvim_tab.rs `PaneLayout`

NOT translated: upstream's Markdown parsing and HTML rendering, which is the
third-party `markdown-it` 4.1.1 and `markdown-it-footnote` 1.0.0 (both MIT,
vendored minified in upstream's lib/). kovan replaces them with
`pulldown-cmark` (already a dependency) using its GFM options, and paints its
own block model into egui. Nor were emojify, highlight.js, CodeMirror, the
spell checker, the codecogs `<equation>` image service (a network call — not
appropriate for an offline tool), localStorage saving, or `github-markdown.css`
(no licence header in upstream's copy; nothing was copied from it).

